{
  "notes": "Nu-disco, Bb major, 116 BPM, a touch of swing. Sampled string stabs on the offbeats (the disco 'chk', held through beat 4), a fat unison synth bass jumping octaves in eighths, the player's sync lead on the Smart Keys, and the DISCO kit: four on the floor, snare and clap on 2 and 4, long open hats on the offbeats, congas and cowbell in the lift, syndrum toms in the fills, the parts pumping on the kick. Scenes: A CLOCK OUT swells IVmaj7 V; B NIGHT BUS turns IVmaj7 V iii7 vi7; C MIRRORBALL climbs ii7 iii7 IVmaj7 V; D LAST TRAIN holds vi7 IVmaj7. ENERGY: strings alone, then kick and bass, then the full disco kit, then sixteenths, fills and ratchets. All material is original.",
